@startuml
' Sources: SIDIS-2026-2027-P1, professor PL2/PL3, PSOFT assignment,
' PSOFT ZIP and output/arq_corrigida.puml. Proposed distributed design.
' Solid arrows: requested operational dependencies. Dashed arrows: additional
' consumers already present in arq_corrigida.puml and supported by PSOFT queries.
' No DDD integration pattern (e.g. Shared Kernel) is assumed without evidence.
title AISafe - DDD Context Map\nProposed distributed architecture
top to bottom direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor white

rectangle "Route / Flight Operations\n\nRoute, RouteHistory, Flight" as Route
rectangle "Aircraft Management\n\nAircraftModel, Aircraft\nAircraftAvailability, AircraftCertification" as Aircraft
rectangle "Airport Management\n\nAirport, Runway, Facilities\nAirportStatus, Certification" as Airport
rectangle "Maintenance Management\n\nMaintenanceTemplate, MaintenanceRecord" as Maintenance

Route -down-> Aircraft : HTTP/REST\nExistence, operational status,\nrange and capacity
Route -down-> Airport : HTTP/REST\nOrigin and destination,\noperational status, certifications
Route -down-> Maintenance : HTTP/REST\nMaintenance status\nand maintenance-related availability
Maintenance --> Aircraft : HTTP/REST\nExistence and minimum required data\n(model and flight hours when needed)
Aircraft ..> Route : HTTP/REST\nCompatible routes, flight queries\nand statistics
Airport ..> Route : HTTP/REST\nAirport routes and statistics

legend bottom left
  Arrows point from the consumer to the information provider.
  Solid: operational dependencies. Dashed: existing reporting/query dependencies.
  Each Bounded Context owns its business logic and data.
  Cross-context dependencies use HTTP/REST; there is no shared database.
  Boundaries follow business responsibilities and DDD principles.
  APIs are proposed: direct cross-context repository access must be replaced.
  Flight represents ScheduledFlight in the current PSOFT code.
  Model-to-airport certification eligibility remains TBD in the current model.
endlegend
@enduml
